{:edb/db-before-t 1242 :edb/db-after-t 1243 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534555 50 #inst "2026-10-12T02:55:47.653Z" 13194139534555 17592186045417 true] [17592186158786 1078 #edb/ref 17592186158787 13194139534555 17592186045417 true] [17592186158804 1078 #edb/ref 17592186158808 13194139534555 17592186045417 true] [17592186162057 1038 #edb/ref 17592186425506 13194139534555 17592186045417 true] [17592186162058 1038 #edb/ref 17592186425505 13194139534555 17592186045417 true] [17592186162264 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534555 17592186045417 true] [17592186162264 1071 "If $Var[X] = 8$, calculate $Var[2X]$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139534555 17592186045417 false] [17592186162264 1071 "If $\\text{Var}[X]=8,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[2X].$" 13194139534555 17592186045417 true] [17592186162264 1074 "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2X] & ={2}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =4\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534555 17592186045417 true] [17592186162267 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534555 17592186045417 true] [17592186162267 1071 "The probability distribution of the random variable $X$ is given below. Given that $E[X] = 7$, calculate $Var[2 - 5X]$.\n\n| $x$ | $5$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ |\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139534555 17592186045417 false] [17592186162267 1071 "The probability distribution of the random variable $X$ is given below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=7,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[2-5X].$ \n\n| $x$ | $5$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ |" 13194139534555 17592186045417 true] [17592186162267 1074 "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constants $a$ and $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+b]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=-5$ and $b=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2-5X] & =(-5)^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =25\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the variance of $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we're given that $\\text{E}[X]=7.$ \n\nWe start by computing $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={5}^{2}\\cdot f(5)+{6}^{2}\\cdot f(6)+{9}^{2}\\cdot f(9) \\\\  & =25(\\frac{1}{5})+36(\\frac{2}{5})+81(\\frac{2}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{259}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{259}{5}-{7}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{259}{5}-49 \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2-5X] & =25\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =25\\cdot \\frac{14}{5} \\\\  & =14\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =70.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534555 17592186045417 true] [17592186425492 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425507 13194139534555 17592186045417 true] [17592186425492 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425508 13194139534555 17592186045417 true] [17592186425492 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425509 13194139534555 17592186045417 true] [17592186425492 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425510 13194139534555 17592186045417 true] [17592186425492 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425511 13194139534555 17592186045417 true] [17592186425492 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534555 17592186045417 true] [17592186425492 1045 "Properties of Variance for Discrete Random Variables" 13194139534555 17592186045417 true] [17592186425492 1046 #edb/ref 17592186425510 13194139534555 17592186045417 true] [17592186425492 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 13194139534555 17592186045417 true] [17592186425492 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048731